Layer C produces the joint credal set $\mathcal{B}$ from observations

O_{\text{orbit}}, O_{\text{attitude}}, O_{\text{mech}}, O_{\text{therm}}, O_{\text{vehicle}}, O_{\text{payload}},

using the mapping of Section 4.2, the correlation model of Section 4.3, and the fusion rules of Sections 4.4–4.7. The map $g_i$ depends on the current plant state $\Sigma^{(k)}$, and so does the residual covariance. This state-dependence is the principal correction of the architecture over earlier drafts, which treated the fusion layer as static while the plant was time-varying.

