\mathcal{S} = (i, \Sigma^{(i)}, A_i, \Sigma^{(i+1)}), \qquad \Sigma^{(i+1)} = f(\Sigma^{(i)}, A_i).

Definition 5.2. The constellation state after $k$ deployments is

\mathcal{C}_k = \big\{ (a_i, e_i, i_i, \Omega_i, \omega_i, M_i, \mathbf{Cov}_i) \big\}_{i=1}^{k}.

5.8 Collision Assessment (Wired In)

Before deployment of payload $i+1$, two obligations are evaluated against the existing constellation $\mathcal{C}_k$:

\mathcal{O}_1(i+1): \quad \max_j P_c(x_{i+1}, x_j) \leq P_{c,\text{screen}} = 10^{-4},

\mathcal{O}_2(i+1): \quad \sum_j P_c(x_{i+1}, x_j) \leq P_{c,\text{aggregate}} = 10^{-3}.

The screening threshold $P_{c,\text{screen}} = 10^{-4}$ is the NASA CARA red threshold used for maneuver decisions (NPR 8079.1). The aggregate budget $P_{c,\text{aggregate}}$ is a placeholder in the order of magnitude of constellation-level conjunction budgets. Both obligations are conjuncts of the authorization predicate and both appear in the formal specification of Chapter 6.

Open Problem 10.4. The correct value and derivation of $P_{c,\text{aggregate}}$ from first principles.

