Chapter 6 — Formal Specification

6.1 State Space

\mathcal{Q} = \mathcal{P} \times \mathcal{D} \times \mathcal{F} \times \mathcal{A} \times \mathcal{E} \times \mathcal{I},

with $\mathcal{D}$ including $\text{DONE}$ and $\mathcal{I} \in \{1, \ldots, N+1\}$.

6.2 Safety Invariants

The following are safety properties, expressed in temporal logic. They must hold in every reachable state.

\begin{aligned}
\text{I1} &:\; \square(D = \text{DEPLOY} \Rightarrow A = \text{AUTHORIZED}) \\
\text{I2} &:\; \square(P = \text{UNCERTAIN} \Rightarrow D = \text{POSTCHECK}) \\
\text{I3} &:\; \square(D = \text{ARMED} \Rightarrow P_{\text{budget}} > P_{\text{min}}) \\
\text{I4} &:\; \square \neg (A = \text{INHIBITED} \land D = \text{DEPLOY}) \\
\text{I5} &:\; \square(D = \text{DEPLOY} \Rightarrow \text{EvidenceOK}) \\
\text{I6} &:\; \square(A = \text{HOLD} \Rightarrow t_{\text{hold}}(i) < t_{\text{hold}}^{\text{max}}(i)) \\
\text{I7} &:\; \square(T(t) \in [T_{\text{min}}, T_{\text{max}}]) \\
\text{I8} &:\; \square(P = \text{SEPARATED} \Rightarrow P_c < P_{c,\text{screen}} \;\forall j) \\
\text{I9} &:\; \square \neg (P = \text{CAPTIVE} \land D = \text{DEPLOY}) \\
\text{I10} &:\; \square(D^{(i+1)} = \text{DEPLOY} \Rightarrow \text{check}(\Sigma_v^{(i+1)}, \mathcal{C}_i)) \\
\text{I11} &:\; \square(D = \text{DEPLOY} \Rightarrow A_{\text{kernel}} = \text{AUTHORIZE}) \\
\text{I12} &:\; \square(D = \text{DEPLOY} \Rightarrow i \leq N) \\
\text{I13} &:\; \square(D = \text{DEPLOY} \Rightarrow \textstyle\sum_j P_c \leq P_{c,\text{aggregate}}) \\
\text{I14} &:\; \square(D = \text{DONE} \Rightarrow i = N + 1)
\end{aligned}

Remark on I5. The continuous-time nested invariant of earlier drafts is not expressible in standard TLA⁺. The discrete version is adopted: EvidenceOK is a state variable that must hold at every state where D = DEPLOY. A hybrid-automaton embedding that captures sub-step variation is deferred to Open Problem 10.14.

6.3 Liveness Properties

Liveness properties are not invariants and are stated separately.

\begin{aligned}
\text{L1} &:\; \text{WF}(\text{DisposalAction}) \Rightarrow \square(\text{ABORT} \Rightarrow \Diamond \text{SAFED}) \\
\text{L2} &:\; \square(D = \text{DEPLOY} \land i \leq N \land \neg \text{Timeout} \Rightarrow \Diamond(P = \text{SEPARATED})) \\
\text{L3} &:\; \square(i = N \land D = \text{DEPLOY} \Rightarrow \Diamond D = \text{DONE})
\end{aligned}

L3 is the terminal-reachability property. It is the formal resolution of the terminal-payload deadlock that was a defect of earlier drafts.

6.4 TLA⁺ Module

The following module is the formal specification. It is syntactically parsable in TLC. Predicates drawn from the evidential layer ($\text{Bel}$, $\text{Pl}$, $m$, $K$, $\rho$, UpdateSigmaV, SafeDisposal) remain abstracted as properly typed CONSTANTS with ASSUME bounds; their instantiation is Open Problem 10.3.

```tla
---------------------------- MODULE Deployment ----------------------------
EXTENDS Naturals, TLC, FiniteSets, Sequences

CONSTANTS N, theta_N, theta_H, theta_U, t_hold_max, Gamma_max,
          P_c_screen, P_c_aggregate

ASSUME N \in Nat /\ N >= 1
ASSUME t_hold_max \in Nat /\ t_hold_max > 0
ASSUME theta_N + theta_H < 1
ASSUME P_c_aggregate >= P_c_screen

CONSTANTS BelLower, PlUpper, mThetaUpper, K_value, rho_max,
          UpdateSigmaV, SafeDisposal

VARIABLES P, D, F, A, i, sigma_v, C, t_hold, EvidenceOK, Conflict,
          SumPc, env_fault

vars == <<P, D, F, A, i, sigma_v, C, t_hold, EvidenceOK, Conflict,
          SumPc, env_fault>>

TypeOK ==
    /\ P \in {"CAPTIVE", "SEPARATING", "SEPARATED", "UNCERTAIN"}
    /\ D \in {"PRECHECK", "ARMED", "DEPLOY", "POSTCHECK", "DONE"}
    /\ F \in {"NOMINAL", "DEGRADED", "FAILED"}
    /\ A \in {"UNAUTHORIZED", "HOLD", "AUTHORIZED", "INHIBITED"}
    /\ i \in 1..N+1
    /\ t_hold \in [1..N+1 -> 0..t_hold_max]
    /\ EvidenceOK \in BOOLEAN
    /\ Conflict \in Nat
    /\ SumPc \in Nat
    /\ env_fault \in {"NONE", "MECH", "THERM", "DEB"}

Init ==
    /\ P = "CAPTIVE"
    /\ D = "PRECHECK"
    /\ F = "NOMINAL"
    /\ A = "UNAUTHORIZED"
    /\ i = 1
    /\ sigma_v = <<>>
    /\ C = {}
    /\ t_hold = [k \in 1..N+1 |-> 0]
    /\ EvidenceOK = TRUE
    /\ Conflict = 0
    /\ SumPc = 0
    /\ env_fault = "NONE"

Environment ==
    \/ /\ env_fault = "NONE"
       /\ env_fault' \in {"MECH", "THERM", "DEB"}
       /\ EvidenceOK' = FALSE
       /\ UNCHANGED <<P, D, F, A, i, sigma_v, C, t_hold, Conflict, SumPc>>
    \/ /\ env_fault = "MECH"
       /\ P = "SEPARATING"
       /\ P' = "UNCERTAIN"
       /\ D' = "POSTCHECK"
       /\ UNCHANGED <<F, A, i, sigma_v, C, t_hold, EvidenceOK, Conflict,
                      SumPc, env_fault>>
    \/ /\ env_fault \in {"MECH", "THERM", "DEB"}
       /\ F' = "DEGRADED"
       /\ UNCHANGED <<P, D, A, i, sigma_v, C, t_hold, EvidenceOK, Conflict,
                      SumPc, env_fault>>

Arm ==
    /\ D = "PRECHECK"
    /\ P = "CAPTIVE"
    /\ F = "NOMINAL"
    /\ EvidenceOK
    /\ Conflict < Gamma_max
    /\ i <= N
    /\ D' = "ARMED"
    /\ A' = "AUTHORIZED"
    /\ t_hold' = [t_hold EXCEPT ![i] = 0]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<P, F, i, sigma_v, C, env_fault, EvidenceOK, Conflict, SumPc>>

Deploy ==
    /\ D = "ARMED"
    /\ A = "AUTHORIZED"
    /\ EvidenceOK
    /\ Conflict < Gamma_max
    /\ SumPc <= P_c_aggregate
    /\ P' = "SEPARATING"
    /\ D' = "DEPLOY"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<F, A, i, sigma_v, C, t_hold, env_fault, EvidenceOK,
                   Conflict, SumPc>>

ConfirmSeparation ==
    /\ P = "SEPARATING"
    /\ D = "DEPLOY"
    /\ i <= N
    /\ P' = "SEPARATED"
    /\ i' = i + 1
    /\ sigma_v' = Append(sigma_v, UpdateSigmaV(sigma_v, i))
    /\ C' = C \cup {i}
    /\ D' = IF i < N THEN "POSTCHECK" ELSE "DONE"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<F, A, t_hold, env_fault, EvidenceOK, Conflict, SumPc>>

ResetAuth ==
    /\ P = "SEPARATED"
    /\ D = "POSTCHECK"
    /\ i <= N
    /\ P' = "CAPTIVE"
    /\ D' = "PRECHECK"
    /\ A' = "UNAUTHORIZED"
    /\ t_hold' = [t_hold EXCEPT ![i] = 0]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<F, i, sigma_v, C, env_fault, EvidenceOK, Conflict, SumPc>>

Timeout ==
    /\ P = "SEPARATING"
    /\ D = "DEPLOY"
    /\ P' = "UNCERTAIN"
    /\ D' = "POSTCHECK"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<F, A, i, sigma_v, C, t_hold, env_fault, EvidenceOK,
                   Conflict, SumPc>>

Hold ==
    /\ A = "HOLD"
    /\ t_hold[i] < t_hold_max
    /\ t_hold' = [t_hold EXCEPT ![i] = t_hold[i] + 1]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<P, D, F, i, sigma_v, C, env_fault, EvidenceOK, Conflict,
                   SumPc>>

Abort ==
    /\ Conflict >= Gamma_max \/ t_hold[i] >= t_hold_max
    /\ D' = "POSTCHECK"
    /\ A' = "INHIBITED"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<P, F, i, sigma_v, C, t_hold, env_fault, EvidenceOK,
                   Conflict, SumPc>>

RecoverFromAbort ==
    /\ D = "POSTCHECK"
    /\ A = "INHIBITED"
    /\ EvidenceOK
    /\ Conflict < Gamma_max
    /\ D' = "PRECHECK"
    /\ A' = "UNAUTHORIZED"
    /\ UNCHANGED <<P, F, i, sigma_v, C, t_hold, env_fault, EvidenceOK,
                   Conflict, SumPc>>

Next ==
    \/ Environment
    \/ Arm \/ Deploy \/ ConfirmSeparation \/ ResetAuth
    \/ Timeout \/ Hold \/ Abort \/ RecoverFromAbort

Fairness ==
    /\ WF_vars(Arm)
    /\ WF_vars(Deploy)
    /\ WF_vars(ConfirmSeparation)
    /\ WF_vars(ResetAuth)
    /\ WF_vars(Timeout)
    /\ WF_vars(Abort)
    /\ WF_vars(RecoverFromAbort)

Spec == Init /\ [][Next]_vars /\ Fairness

Inv_Auth          == [](D = "DEPLOY" => A = "AUTHORIZED")
Inv_Uncertainty   == [](P = "UNCERTAIN" => D = "POSTCHECK")
Inv_HoldBound     == [](A = "HOLD" => t_hold[i] < t_hold_max)
Inv_Evidence      == [](D = "DEPLOY" => EvidenceOK)
Inv_NoCaptive     == []~(P = "CAPTIVE" /\ D = "DEPLOY")
Inv_IndexBound    == [](D = "DEPLOY" => i <= N)
Inv_AggregatePc   == [](D = "DEPLOY" => SumPc <= P_c_aggregate)
Inv_TerminalShape == [](D = "DONE" => i = N + 1)

Prop_Termination  == <>(D = "DONE")
Prop_Disposal     == WF_vars(Abort) => [](A = "INHIBITED" => <>SafeDisposal)
=============================================================================
```

6.5 Properties of the Specification

The specification is designed so that the following properties hold:

· P1. No authorization is inherited across payloads: ResetAuth is the only action that transitions from $\text{SEPARATED}$ back to $\text{CAPTIVE}$, and it forces $A = \text{UNAUTHORIZED}$.
· P2. The sequence terminates: ConfirmSeparation when $i = N$ transitions $D$ to $\text{DONE}$, and $i$ increments to $N+1$.
· P3. The Environment action can force any action precondition false: it can set EvidenceOK' = FALSE, degrade F, or force P = UNCERTAIN from SEPARATING. Invariants are therefore non-vacuous with respect to the environment.
· P4. The hold counter is per-payload: t_hold is a function of the payload index, so the HOLD invariant is not vacuously true in the inter-payload interval.

6.6 Scalability

For $N = 26$ and $|\mathcal{Q}| = 4 \times 5 \times 3 \times 4 = 240$, the naive state space is $240^{26}$, infeasible. Assume-guarantee contract decomposition is adopted following NASA practice: phase-specific contracts define assumptions on inputs and guarantees on outputs, and each contract is verified in isolation before composition. The DLR demonstration of symbolic model checking to 250 state machines supports the tractability of the per-phase verification.

