7.2 Quantitative Safety Case Requirements

A compliant safety case would require: FMECA for each subsystem; FTA for top-level hazardous events; quantitative failure rates for mechanical, electrical, and software components; single-failure-point analysis; and common-cause failure quantification for the dissimilar redundancy claims. None of these is provided by this dissertation, which is a theoretical architecture, not a safety case.

7.3 Common-Cause Failure Mitigation

Three mitigations are proposed.

Mitigation 7.1. Deploy DSK in a dissimilar environment: different OS (e.g., seL4 with formal proof of functional correctness), different compiler, different memory domain, diverse algorithms for critical functions, formal dissimilarity proof.

Mitigation 7.2. Independent hardware monitor: FPGA-based watchdog with formally verified specification that can veto any deployment command.

Mitigation 7.3. N-version voting with known consensus failure modes, using algorithms from independent specification teams.

7.4 Disposal Policy

Obligation 7.1. For each satellite in the constellation, apply the FCC 5-year rule only if the satellite was launched on or after 29 September 2024 (FCC 22-74 effective date). Pre-2024 satellites are grandfathered under the 25-year guideline. The disposal sub-state is assigned per-satellite according to this filter.

